    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49419" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῡμο-φθόρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>destroying the soul,
				life-destroying</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάρμακα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.329
				</span></i>
			 (so, metaph. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γράψας ἐν πίνακι θυμοφθόρα πολλά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.169
				</span></i>
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					140
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυιοφθ-</span>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>heart-breaking</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν δ᾽ ἄχος
				ἀμφεχύθη θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.716
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.363
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πενίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					717
				</span></i>
			; of persons, <i>troublesome, annoying</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.323
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμοβόρος</span>.</div>
